# Git Workflow
After you have completed a task and all tests/verifications pass, you MUST:
1. Run `git add .`
2. Generate a commit message using the Conventional Commits format.
3. Run `git commit -m "your generated message"`

## Commit hygiene
- Run `git status --short` before `git add .` and confirm every staged path is intentional.
  Untracked scratch files (logs, temp exports, download leftovers) must be deleted or added
  to `.gitignore` — never committed.
- One logical change per commit.
- `reports/` (gdUnit4 output) and Godot `~*` atomic-write temp files are gitignored. Never
  `git add -f` them.

## Pushing (main is protected — never push to it directly)
`main` requires the `validate` and `Scripts and tests` status checks, and a required check
must be *reported* before `main` accepts a commit — so `git push origin main` fails with
`GH006: 2 of 2 required status checks are expected`. The checks cannot exist for a commit
that has never been pushed, and `enforce_admins` is on, so do not try to force it. Land the
work through a branch and a pull request:

1. `git switch -c <type>/<short-name>` then `git push -u origin <type>/<short-name>`
2. `gh pr create --base main --head <type>/<short-name> --title "<subject>" --body "<summary>"`
3. `gh pr checks <n>` until `validate` and `Scripts and tests` are green (`Resolve Godot
   version` also runs, but it is not a required context)
4. `gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch` — `--merge`, not `--squash`, so every
   Conventional Commit stays its own commit on `main` (linear history is not required)
5. `git switch main; git pull --ff-only` and confirm `git status -sb` shows no ahead/behind

## Pre-flight gates (required before every commit)
Run all eight gates from the repo root — they are exactly the gates CI runs:

1. Validate game data (errors **and** warnings are fatal):
   `godot --headless --path . "res://Tools/validator.tscn" -- --strict`
2. Compile every script:
   `godot --headless --path . --script res://Tools/check_scripts.gd`
3. Navigation index checks — coverage, ranges, links, scenes, signals, data, staleness,
   plus a read-cost benchmark:
   `godot --headless --path . --script res://Tools/check_navigation.gd`
4. Unit tests:
   `godot --headless --path . -s res://addons/gdUnit4/bin/GdUnitCmdTool.gd -a res://GDTest -c --ignoreHeadlessMode`
5. Anti-slop lint — bans `create_timer()`, frame pumps and upward tree walks,
   keeps `Core/` pure logic, and ratchets file lines, function lines, a function's
   branch score (1 + one point per `if`/`elif`/`for`/`while`/`match`) and
   `get_parent()` calls per file against `Tools/slop_baseline.json` (baseline
   entries may only shrink). `--strict` makes a stale entry fail instead of warn:
   `python Tools/line_godot_slop.py --strict`
6. Python tooling tests — one dependency-free `Tools/<module>_test.py` suite per Python
   tool, each in the shape of `Tools/rig_combat_actor_test.py`. A gate nobody tests is a
   gate that silently stops gating, and a wrong denominator in the report would not
   crash — it would answer the wrong question convincingly:
   `python Tools/line_godot_slop_test.py`
   `python Tools/analyze_telemetry_test.py`
   `python Tools/rig_combat_actor_test.py`
7. Replay a seed — the CLI a telemetry or bug report's seed is reproduced with, over the
   shipped battle, asserting the board's invariants at every decision:
   `godot --headless --path . res://Tools/simulate_runs.tscn -- --seeds 3`
8. Migration parity — applies `Server/supabase/migrations/001`–`006` in order to a real
   PostgreSQL server and then asserts what every view answers, so a migration that
   cannot be pushed fails here instead of at deploy time. It is how `004`'s
   `create or replace view` column-order bug was found: `create or replace view` may
   only *append* columns, so `004` never applied to a fresh database and `supabase db
   push` stopped there. Skipped with a printed notice when `psql` is absent; CI always
   runs it:
   `psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -d <scratch-db> -f Server/supabase/tests/migrations_test.sql`

Never commit past a red gate. If a gate fails, fix the root cause — do not weaken the gate.
If gate 3 fails because the index is stale, regenerate it (`Docs/` is generated — never
hand-edit it); on Windows `pwsh -File Tools/preflight.ps1 -FixIndex` regenerates it and then
runs every gate.

Before changing UI or scenes, look at the pixels (the headless gates cannot):
`godot --audio-driver Dummy --position -4000,-4000 --path . res://Tools/snapshot_runner.tscn`
renders `reports/ui-snapshots/` (seeded battle, real OpenGL, `manifest.json`).

## Second-pass review (required before opening a PR)
Run the diff reviewer and fix what it flags before you push — do not open a PR and let
the human be the first reader of your own diff:

`godot --headless --path . --script res://Tools/review_diff.gd -- --base origin/main --strict`

It leads with the **blast radius**: `high` when trunk code moved (`Core/`, `Managers/`, the
EventBus, `Data/json/config.json`, `project.godot`, CI, or any script the generated map shows
many others depend on — the fan-in is read off `Docs/map/<path>.md`), `medium` for leaf game
code, `low` for tests/tools/docs only. Read the high tier line by line; skim the low one once
the gates are green. It also reports whether a staged feature flag bounds the change.

`--strict` fails on `undocumented_api`, `core_purity` and `assertionless_test` (a newly added
`GDTest/` `test_*` method with no assertion — a test that cannot fail is coverage theatre).
`untested_change`, `banned_pattern`, `todo_added`, `unstaged_rollout`, `oversize_diff` and
`large_file_change` are advisory: this repo names suites by behaviour, so a filename match for
"did this change come with a test" would be wrong as often as it is right. Read the advisory
list before pushing and decide.
Commit first: the reviewer diffs the branch against the base, so it reads what is committed.
CI runs the same reviewer without `--strict` and posts it as a sticky PR comment.
Add `--adversarial` to append the context-isolated brief — the invariants a *fresh* reviewer
should attack plus the files whose map pages belong in its context; hand that, the diff and
`AGENTS.md` to a reviewer that never saw the authoring conversation. CI passes it too,
collapsed inside `<details>` so the sticky comment stays one screenful. A change that touches
`Scenes/` or `Shaders/` also carries a `Visual proof: required` line, because the headless
gates rasterise nothing — the snapshot is the proof.
`pwsh -File Tools/preflight.ps1 -Review` runs every gate plus this review.

## Forward pressure (task intake)
Turn evidence into work instead of noticing it by hand. One command prints
agent-ready task specs (title, evidence, repro, acceptance):

`godot --headless --path . --script res://Tools/triage.gd`

Add `--report report.json` (written by `python Tools/analyze_telemetry.py --json report.json`)
for the telemetry signals, `--json tasks.json` to dump them, and `--create` to file
them as `agent-task` issues. Filing is idempotent: every spec carries a stable marker.
The weekly `Task Intake` workflow runs the repo-side sources only, and files nothing
unless it is dispatched with `file_issues`.

## Context budget (explore without reading everything)
- **Read `Docs/CODEBASE_MAP.md` first.** It is generated and deliberately small: section 1 lists
  every game script, section 2 every test, section 3 every `EventBus` signal with its emitters and
  listeners, section 4 the scenes, and section 5 the JSON data shapes and keys.
- **Per-script detail is one page:** `Docs/map/<path>.md` holds signals, constants, exports,
  onready nodes and the public API with line ranges plus `Uses` / `Used by`; the `*.scene.md`
  pages hold the scene node trees.
- **Look symbols up instead of grepping blindly:**
  `rg -n '^my_symbol\t' Docs/symbols.tsv` returns `path:start-end` in a single line.
- **Then open only that range** — never read a whole file to find one function, and never read
  `addons/` or `Trash/` unless the task is about them.
- **Regenerate after any code, scene or data change:**
  `godot --headless --path . --script res://Tools/gen_code_index.gd`
- **Measure the recipes instead of guessing:**
  `godot --headless --path . --script res://Tools/check_navigation.gd -- --benchmark` prints the
  bytes and estimated tokens each documented recipe reads versus opening the source files.

## Terminal environment (Windows / PowerShell 7)
- The default integrated terminal is PowerShell 7 from `$env:USERPROFILE\Tools\PowerShell7`
  (upgraded from PS 5.1, whose shell integration never reported command completion).
- A freshly opened shell may carry a stale PATH. If `pwsh`, `rg`, `fd`, `uv`, `gh`, `node`,
  `gdformat` or `jq` are "not recognized", prepend the user-space toolchain:
  `$env:Path = "$env:USERPROFILE\Tools\PowerShell7;$env:USERPROFILE\Tools\bin;$env:USERPROFILE\.local\bin;C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI;C:\Program Files\nodejs;C:\ffmpeg;" + [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('Path','Machine')`
- `gh` is installed **and authenticated** as `Cookieoil` (token scopes `gist`, `read:org`,
  `repo`, `workflow`), so `gh pr create`, `gh pr checks`, `gh pr merge`, `gh run list` and
  `gh api` work as-is; re-run `gh auth login` only if `gh auth status` reports otherwise.
- For long-running installs/downloads, start a detached process that logs to a file:
  `Start-Process -WindowStyle Hidden -FilePath powershell.exe -ArgumentList '-NoProfile','-ExecutionPolicy','Bypass','-File','<script.ps1>'`
  then poll the log with the read tool. Do not block the terminal; it has no reliable
  completion signal for long commands.
- **`Start-Process -ArgumentList` never quotes.** It joins array elements with spaces, so an
  argument containing a space is silently split — passing `'-Godot','C:\Program Files (x86)\...\godot.exe'`
  reaches the child as `-Godot C:\Program`, and `Tools/preflight.ps1` exits with
  `Godot executable not found: C:\Program`. Give the path element its own quotes instead:
  `$g = '"C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Godot Engine\godot.exe"'; Start-Process pwsh -ArgumentList '-NoProfile','-ExecutionPolicy','Bypass','-File','Tools/preflight.ps1','-Godot',$g`
- **A detached child inherits the *session* PATH.** Prepending the user-space toolchain above
  drops Steam's `godot.exe` entry, so a detached `pwsh -File Tools/preflight.ps1` exits at once
  with `Godot executable not found: godot`; pass `-Godot` explicitly to sidestep it.
- Prefer `curl.exe` over `Invoke-WebRequest` (PS 5.1 uses the IE engine and can hang).
